ew venue in the Yenikent district. The stadium was named after the date May 19, 1919, when Mustafa Kemal Atatürk arrived at Samsun to start the Turkish War of Independence. Official ceremonies to celebrate the May 19th Youth and Sports Day were also held\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d01\", \"text\": \"The Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium () was the home venue of Bursaspor. It was built in 1930 and is part of the 19 Mayıs Sports Complex, which is located in the Ulus district. The stadium had a capacity of 19,209 (all-seater). Ankaraspor also used the stadium until they moved to their new venue in the Yenikent district. The stadium was named after the date May 19, 1919, when Mustafa Kemal Atatürk arrived at Samsun to start the Turkish War of Independence. Official ceremonies to celebrate the May 19th Youth and Sports Day were also held here.\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d02\", \"text\": \"Fisht Olympic Stadium Forest Arena Frank Clair Stadium Friends Arena Gamba Osaka Stadium Gaziantep Arena Generali-Arena Gewiss Stadium Ghelamco Arena Gillette Stadium Giresun Çotanak Stadyumu Gradski Stadion GFK Dubočica Gradski Stadion Lagator Grand Stade de Tétouan Grand Stade du Havre Grand Stade Lille Grêmio Arena Gürsel Aksel Stadyumu Haladás Stadion Hangzhou Sports Park Stadium Hard Rock Stadium Hatay Stadi Hayward Field Hazza Bin Zayed Stadium Hidegkuti Nándor Stadion Hietalahden Stadion Hiroshima Peace Stadium Houston Football Stadium Hwaseong Sports Complex Hypo-Arena Illovszky Stadion Impuls-Arena Incheon Asiad Main Stadium Independência Investors Group Field Izmit Stadi Jaber Al-Ahmad International Stadium Jakarta International Stadium\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"Samsunspor\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"19 Mayıs Stadium in Samsun is historically the home of Samsunspor. However, due to frequent club restructurings and name changes, I am slightly uncertain about its current exclusive tenant without real-time verification.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium\", \"scope\": \"home venue\", \"claim\": \"The Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium was the home venue of Ankara's Gençlerbirliği.\", \"answer\": \"Gençlerbirliği\", \"quote\": \"Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium The Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium () was the home venue of Ankara's Gençlerbirliği.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d00:c1\", \"entity\": \"Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium\", \"scope\": \"used the stadium\", \"claim\": \"Ankaraspor also used the stadium until they moved to their new venue in the Yenikent district.\", \"answer\": \"Ankaraspor\", \"quote\": \"Ankaraspor also used the stadium until they moved to their new venue in the Yenikent district.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Bursaspor\", \"scope\": \"sports team\", \"claim\": \"The Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium was the home venue of Bursaspor.\", \"answer\": \"Bursaspor\", \"quote\": \"The Ankara 19 Mayıs Stadium () was the home venue of Bursaspor.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0061-ad512dd8e450:d01:c1\", \"entity\": \"Ankaraspor\", \"scope\": \"sports team\", \"claim\": \"Ankaraspor also used the stadium until they moved to their new venue in the Yenikent district.\", \"answer\": \"Ankaraspor\", \"quote\": \"Ankaraspor also used the stadium until they moved to their new venue in the Yenikent district.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}]}"
